  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 101 AM EDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nThe upper level low mentioned above will eventually get absorbed \ninto the broader upper level flow early in the week. Then a frontal \nboundary will slide down the state the middle to end of the work \nweek. This will keep rain chances elevated through the extended \nperiod. WPC has some fairly robust rainfall totals each day, \nespecially from the middle to end of the work week. 7 day totals of \n5-7 inches are fairly reasonable given the above average moisture in \nplace across the area. Given antecedent conditions, flooding will \nremain the primary concern across the metro areas throughout the \nweek. \n\nTemperatures will remain near normal through the end of the week, \nwith highs generally in the upper 80s to lower 90s. Low temps each \nnight will be in the lower 70s over the interior, to mid and upper \n70s across the metro.",
